    "notes": [
      "Base class slots exclude domain, school and spirit slots. Null means no table entry; zero means bonus spells only.",
      "The Bard journal repeats its per-day table in place of spells known. Shared medium spells known use Hunter and Summoner, cross-checked against Pathfinder Unchained Tables 1–4 and 1–5.",
      "The journal spells the Medium heading Mediuum; its known table supplies the low spontaneous zero-level column. Classes without cantrips ignore that column.",
      "Occultist has no fixed spells-known count: implement-school choices determine it. Its override deliberately omits spellsKnown.",
      "Adept has a finite zero-level per-day column and no Cantrips or Orisons class feature (CRB pp. 448–449); its reviewed cantrips=false corrects the Foundry casting summary, while its table retains three zero-level spells per day.",
      "Adept, extract and Unchained summoner overrides are transcribed from the reviewed pf1-spellcasting-rules corpus (CRB p. 448, APG p. 26, ACG p. 30, PU p. 25).",
      "Occultist rows explicitly include zero-level knack availability in castableSpellLevels, while omitting a fixed spellsKnown count.",
      "Book collection types follow the class recording rules: alchemist formula books (APG pp. 26–27), investigator formula books (ACG pp. 30–31), and witch familiars (APG pp. 65–67)."
    ]
  },
